Desktop pet

Keep DeepSeek Whale by your side and get a reminder when a task finishes or needs your attention. The interface follows the Harness language, using the system language when no preference is set.

Pet status
Visible

Unexpected exits retry a limited number of times. You can restart manually after failure. Hidden pets follow system notification settings. Window drafts are lost when the process exits.

Show pet
Hide pet
Restart
Close pet
Preferences
Start with Harness

Open the pet automatically the next time Harness starts.

Roam when idle

Move slowly across the current screen while idle.

Daily rhythm

Off by default. With idle roaming on, act every 45–90 seconds by day, gently every 2–4 minutes at 22:00–07:00 local time. Work, reading, input, rest and reduced motion take priority.

Task notifications

Remind you about completion, errors, approvals and AI questions.

Local diagnostics

Off by default. Allow a separate local sampler to read resource and activity counts without chat content. Turn off to stop providing data.

Companionship

Quiet companionship adds daily routines; interactive companionship occasionally invites you. Shared activities unlock a familiar greeting. Work and reading take priority.

Off (legacy rhythm)
Quiet
Interactive
Home position (%)

Relative to the current work area, constrained by actual body bounds.

Exploration range (%)

Explore along the bottom of this display. Automatic activity permission still controls departures.

Character size

90–240 pixels. Changes apply immediately.

Text size

100%, 125% or 150%, independently of character size. Applies immediately and keeps your reading and draft.

100%
125%
150%
Bubble duration

2–60 seconds. Hover or focus pauses dismissal; pending requests stay in the list.

Saved

Reminders and notifications
System notifications

Harness sends system notifications while the pet is hidden. A visible pet presents reminders itself.

Pending request reminders

Remind once when an approval or AI question remains pending. You can also snooze it.

Reminder delay

1–1440 minutes, default 10 minutes.

Web notification permission: Not requested · OS authorization awaits verification

macOS: System Settings → Notifications → DeepSeek Harness. Windows: Settings → System → Notifications. Linux: desktop notification settings. For local web, check browser notification settings. Use a test notification to verify OS delivery after granting web permission.

Request / refresh permission
Test system notification

Enable task and system notifications, then hide the running pet to send a test.

